<!--
  Android 16 overlay on the LineageOS 23.0 manifest.

  NO PROJECTS LEFT, and empty rather than deleted — for the same two reasons as the A17 overlay
  beside it, which this file now mirrors exactly.

  Empty, because A16 no longer syncs anything from an upstream container project (bd remora-28ix.4). This file
  used to add five projects: the upstream device tree, its prebuilts, its vendor project and
  its OMX and c2 components. Every one is replaced the way A17 replaced it —
  device/remora and vendor/remora are STAGED into the tree by stage-device-tree.sh rather than
  synced, because no manifest can provide Remora-authored source and pointing a remote at one
  machine's disk made the build unreproducible everywhere else; mesa_source supplies the GL and
  Vulkan stack those prebuilts packaged; the OMX plugin gated on a boot arg
  Remora has never emitted; and the c2 service wiring lives in Remora's own hardware/remora/c2-va.

  Not deleted, because the engine requires it to exist. SourceBuild.cpp's unpinned path copies
  `<source-build>/local_manifests/remora-a<ver>*.xml` and Chain.cpp preflights that glob, so
  removing the file breaks unpinned A16 builds with a missing-manifest error rather than doing
  nothing. An overlay with no projects IS the correct overlay now: repo reads it, adds nothing, and
  the tree is stock LineageOS plus the staged Remora trees. Keep it in step with
  pinned-manifest-a16.xml — that one is the reproducible pin, this is the tip-tracking overlay, and
  a project present in only one of them makes the build depend on which manifest was used.

  Base tree:  repo init -u https://github.com/LineageOS/android.git -b lineage-23.0
  Lunch:      remora_x86_64-bp2a-userdebug
-->
<manifest>
</manifest>
